      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your guilt stems from a desire to make amends for the harm caused, but redemption often begins when we take full responsibility and actively support the recovery of those we wronged rather than punishing ourselves with isolation. While the damage may feel permanent in the moment, healing trajectories exist even when the consequences are severe, often requiring us to rebuild trust slowly instead of waiting for perfection. Please consider speaking with a licensed therapist who can walk with you through processing these intense feelings without forcing you to carry the entire weight alone.",
